Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:05.474
Hey YouTubers! It's Charlie. So this is going to be my Game of Thrones episode two video.

00:00:05.474 --> 00:00:08.820
Generally I think this episode is a lot more fun than episode one.

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:11.440
We're finally getting into some of the action of the season.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.560
We get to see two big new locations

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:16.808
We also get to see some really fun familiar faces.

00:00:16.808 --> 00:00:19.340
Careful for spoilers from the episode if you haven't seen it yet.

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:21.340
And new round of the giveaway starts now.

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:25.049
All you have to do to enter is be a subscriber and leave a comment on this video.

00:00:25.049 --> 00:00:27.013
It's for an HBO Now subscription.

00:00:27.013 --> 00:00:28.900
So here we go starting with top five moments.

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:32.000
Number five: Arya goes to the house of Black and White.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.400
If you remember the last time we saw The Titan of Braavos

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:37.420
It was when Stannis was going to get money from the Iron Bank.

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:40.133
I love how she laughs at the myth of The Titan.

00:00:40.133 --> 00:00:43.154
You can tell that she doesn't care about faith. She's not a religious person.

00:00:43.154 --> 00:00:46.000
I'll be interested to see how that changes, or if that changes

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:48.035
during her time with the Faceless Men.

00:00:48.035 --> 00:00:51.115
I think they redid some of the CG for the city too, the city shots.

00:00:51.115 --> 00:00:52.000
I mean obviously

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.693
We move through the camera. We move through the city so we see a couple of the different districts.

00:00:55.693 --> 00:01:00.594
But the big wide CG shot just seems a lot nicer than the one during season four that we saw.

00:01:00.594 --> 00:01:04.955
There's only ten episodes this season so I do think there are a lot of places in Braavos

00:01:04.955 --> 00:01:08.854
that we just won't see. It's the same deal with Meereen. Like you only see certain places.

00:01:08.854 --> 00:01:11.000
Cersei sent Mace Tyrell on a mission

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:15.165
to get more money from the Iron Bank so I do think that we'll see the Iron Bank again.

00:01:15.165 --> 00:01:19.040
This character that she meets here looks like it's the Kindly Man from the books.

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:22.260
Although technically the first face that the Kindly Man shows her

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:25.760
is more of like a skeleton with scraps of skin hanging off of it.

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:28.974
He even has a worm crawling out of his eye that Arya has to kiss.

00:01:28.974 --> 00:01:31.500
It's like her way of showing that she's not afraid.

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:36.330
In the episode I think her standing up to those street thugs kind of took the place of that thematically. 

00:01:36.330 --> 00:01:40.376
Did anyone else think it was curious that when she was saying her prayer outside on the steps,

00:01:40.376 --> 00:01:41.680
she said The Mountain's name.

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:45.674
The whole list is actually very long so we're actually only hearing a small part of it.

00:01:45.674 --> 00:01:49.028
And the mountain yes, who wonders what he's going to do with that head?

00:01:49.028 --> 00:01:52.080
Probably just experiment on it. Maybe harvest it for stuff.

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:54.520
Because there's a bunch of Mountain related stuff

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:57.880
in the books, I'm going to wait till we see more of what the show is going to do. 

00:01:57.880 --> 00:01:59.800
I just don't want to get too crazy into spoilers so

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:04.115
please use spoiler tags if you want to talk about the Mountain or Robert Strong from the books.

00:02:04.115 --> 00:02:06.314
On to number four: Pod and Brienne are like

00:02:06.314 --> 00:02:08.834
every freaking chicken from season four.

00:02:08.834 --> 00:02:10.794
I feel kind of bad for Brienne. It's like

00:02:10.794 --> 00:02:15.180
every Stark child that she runs into just gives her the business and tells her to get out.

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:18.275
She did tell them the story of the smoke baby which was kind of fun.

00:02:18.275 --> 00:02:20.700
You can't really tell if Littlefinger believes her.

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:24.540
I think he just wants to get rid of her. She's like a wild card that he just doesn't want to deal with.

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:26.914
It was kind of hard to tell what Sansa was thinking.

00:02:26.914 --> 00:02:31.174
Maybe she just feels like Brienne reminds her of all the awful things that have happened to her family

00:02:31.174 --> 00:02:32.580
and she just doesn't want to deal with it.

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:34.534
It's not that she likes Littlefinger

00:02:34.534 --> 00:02:38.020
it's just that she's kind of grown comfortable with their situation and their

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:39.828
weird alliance that they have formed

00:02:39.828 --> 00:02:41.894
and she doesn't want to deal with Brienne either.

00:02:41.894 --> 00:02:44.820
As much as it seems like Sansa trusts Littlefinger,

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:47.754
I don't think that she does. I think that she's like slowly wising up

00:02:47.754 --> 00:02:49.654
to the fact that she can't trust anybody.

00:02:49.654 --> 00:02:53.274
Right now for her I think it's more of a "devil you know" situation.

00:02:53.274 --> 00:02:57.733
She still has a lot to learn though before she can survive on her own, without Littlefinger's help.

00:02:57.733 --> 00:03:02.440
It also didn't help Brienne's cause that she was wearing Lannister gear with a Valyrian blade.

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:04.694
But her speech was amazingly sincere.

00:03:04.694 --> 00:03:07.440
Brienne is one of those heart breaking characters that's just

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:09.660
utterly sincere in everything she does but

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:12.214
just constantly gets kicked in the mud.

00:03:12.214 --> 00:03:15.068
I know everyone is asking about Lady Stoneheart this season.

00:03:15.068 --> 00:03:19.119
I still don't expect to see her. I think when she and Pod got separated

00:03:19.119 --> 00:03:20.895
and Pod ended up in the river,

00:03:20.895 --> 00:03:24.280
you could look at that as like an easter egg for Lady Stoneheart

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:27.834
just because we're right around that time in the books when she shows up.

00:03:27.834 --> 00:03:31.520
I'm not expecting it but that doesn't mean it won't happen.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:33.080
You guys can let me know whether you agree.

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:37.116
Do you think that Brienne is stupid for wanting to pursue Sansa to try and help her

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:39.520
even though Sansa wants to have nothing to do with her.

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:42.640
Should she just cut her loses and try to go back and serve with Jaime?

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:46.674
If she really wanted she could probably be named to The King's Guard by Tommen.

00:03:46.674 --> 00:03:48.394
She'd have to do a little bit of convincing

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:50.374
and Cersei might not be super happy about it

00:03:50.374 --> 00:03:53.313
but it seems like something that's never going to happen. Like total FanFic.

00:03:53.313 --> 00:03:58.174
On to number three. Cersei and Jaime decide that Jaime is going to go to Dorne to get Myrcella.

00:03:58.174 --> 00:04:01.320
If you're wondering who sent that message, who sent that threat

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:03.814
it's probably Ellaria Sand. She's the one that's

00:04:03.814 --> 00:04:05.993
trying to start a war with the Lannisters.

00:04:05.993 --> 00:04:08.134
They've changed a whole lot about the Sand snakes so I think

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:11.480
Ellaria Sand is Arienne Martell from the books

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:13.495
with a little bit of Obara Sand too.

00:04:13.495 --> 00:04:16.654
We didn't see them in this episode so I'm just going to wait until next week to talk about

00:04:16.654 --> 00:04:18.835
what the show is doing with the Sand Snakes.

00:04:18.835 --> 00:04:22.533
Cersei tells Jaime that Myrcella is being kept at The Water Gardens.

00:04:22.533 --> 00:04:26.280
The Water Gardens are where Prince Doran Martell has been hiding himself

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:29.532
just so his subjects don't see how bad his gout has gotten.

00:04:29.532 --> 00:04:31.640
He just doesn't want them to see him as weak.

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:34.360
It's so much fun seeing Dr. Bashir Martell.

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:36.214
I'm a big fan of Alexander Siddig.

00:04:36.214 --> 00:04:38.267
He said something really interesting about

00:04:38.267 --> 00:04:40.374
his performance as Doran Martell.

00:04:40.374 --> 00:04:43.046
He said he's basing a lot of the way he speaks his accent

00:04:43.046 --> 00:04:45.654
on what Pedro Pascal did in season four.

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:47.595
It's just that inside the universe of the show

00:04:47.595 --> 00:04:50.094
Pedro Pascal originated the Martell characters

00:04:50.094 --> 00:04:53.774
so all the other actors that are member of his family, the Martell family,

00:04:53.774 --> 00:04:54.934
have to take cues from that.

00:04:54.934 --> 00:04:57.480
He's going to be a lot of fun. What I'm really hoping is

00:04:57.480 --> 00:04:59.680
we see some of his character in season five

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:02.120
and he becomes a much bigger character in season six

00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:04.295
the same thing that they did with Ellaria Sand.

00:05:04.295 --> 00:05:06.734
Areo Hotah is going to be a lot of fun too.

00:05:06.734 --> 00:05:12.040
I would say after Oberyn Martell vs. The Mountain the next biggest fight that I would like to see would be

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:13.580
Bronn vs. Areo.

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:16.654
I don't know if things will go down that way but if there's any two people

00:05:16.654 --> 00:05:19.093
in Westeros that I'd like to see fight it would be those two.

00:05:19.093 --> 00:05:23.435
On to number two. Daenerys tries to figure out what to do with the Sons of the Harpy. 

00:05:23.435 --> 00:05:26.720
So they capture one but then one of her freed slaves

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:30.234
executes him and she's forced to execute him in the name of justice.

00:05:30.234 --> 00:05:35.189
It's this whole big thing about her trying to be more of a diplomat vs. a tyrant like her father.

00:05:35.189 --> 00:05:37.560
It's funny that she doesn't know a lot about her father.

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:41.335
She says Viserys told her things but he probably didn't tell her the whole truth.

00:05:41.335 --> 00:05:45.134
The Mad King. Lots of wild fire. Did not end well for anyone.

00:05:45.134 --> 00:05:48.079
Barristan pretty much narrates Robert's Rebellion for her.

00:05:48.079 --> 00:05:52.654
The rebellion didn't start so much because of Lyanna Stark being supposedly kidnapped,

00:05:52.654 --> 00:05:56.334
by Rhaegar Targaryen even though I think that he didn't kidnap her in the first place.

00:05:56.334 --> 00:05:58.815
What happened is The Mad King killed a bunch of nobels

00:05:58.815 --> 00:06:02.295
and those nobel families banded together and started the rebellion.

00:06:02.295 --> 00:06:04.354
Robert Baratheon was just the point man.

00:06:04.354 --> 00:06:06.435
He was just the person everyone rallied behind.

00:06:06.435 --> 00:06:10.654
So it wasn't the entire kingdom going to war over a woman being kidnapped.

00:06:10.654 --> 00:06:13.760
It looks the Daenerys is facing the same situation

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:16.674
like things are going to descend to civil war inside Meereen.

00:06:16.674 --> 00:06:19.983
We're only in episode two so expect things to escalate. 

00:06:19.983 --> 00:06:25.074
And isn't it funny how Barristan called out wild fire and then we see Drogon at the end of the episode.

00:06:25.074 --> 00:06:27.965
He looks big enough to ride. Definately big enough to ride.

00:06:27.965 --> 00:06:32.940
That would be a really quick way to solve all of her problems. Just roast all of the people yelling at her.

00:06:32.940 --> 00:06:35.560
Finally my number one WTF moment:

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:38.580
Jaqen H'ghar reveals himself to Arya.

00:06:38.582 --> 00:06:40.220
This is a really big departure from the books.

00:06:40.220 --> 00:06:43.764
The Kindly Man, the person who Jaqen was masquerading as

00:06:43.764 --> 00:06:45.494
people thought he might be Jaqen H'ghar.

00:06:45.494 --> 00:06:51.273
but technically Jaqen H'ghar in the books is off on another mission doing something else on the other side of the world.

00:06:51.273 --> 00:06:56.563
So I think we can assume they're cutting out pretty much all of the Citadel plot in season five.

00:06:56.563 --> 00:06:59.877
If you don't know what I'm talking about, don't worry it doesn't matter for the show.

00:06:59.877 --> 00:07:04.233
Jaqen H'ghar gonna teach her the way of the warrior. The way of the faceless warrior.

00:07:04.233 --> 00:07:08.314
I'd say generally of all the running story lines right now that I'm most excited about

00:07:08.454 --> 00:07:10.934
it's Jaime and Bronn headed to Dorne, 

00:07:10.934 --> 00:07:14.753
yay for Lollys. I'm so glad that Lollys is back. That was such a funny scene with Bronn.

00:07:14.753 --> 00:07:16.994
And Arya learning to become a Faceless Man.

00:07:16.994 --> 00:07:20.174
Just as a bonus we have to address Jon Snow becoming Lord Commander.

00:07:20.174 --> 00:07:22.835
This should have been like a top six moments but anyways

00:07:22.835 --> 00:07:25.606
Jon Snow Lord Commander right out of the books. Samwell

00:07:25.606 --> 00:07:28.485
conspires with the other brothers to elect him.

00:07:28.485 --> 00:07:31.454
I love how Maester Aemon was the one that cast the deciding vote.

00:07:31.454 --> 00:07:35.513
I know a lot of you are disappointed that Jon didn't take Stannis' deal to become a Stark,

00:07:35.513 --> 00:07:39.914
that will come back around eventually I think. It wasn't like a one time deal.

00:07:39.914 --> 00:07:42.713
His sense of duty will continue to be tested.

00:07:42.713 --> 00:07:45.568
Here's my big question for you guys: what was your favorite moment from the episode

00:07:45.568 --> 00:07:50.380
and what do you think it's gonna take for Jon Snow to take Stannis' deal?

00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:52.915
To legitimize him and become Jon Stark.

00:07:52.915 --> 00:07:56.374
If Arya isn't going to be able to give up her past life and become

00:07:56.380 --> 00:07:58.640
"no one" as Jaqen implied

00:07:58.640 --> 00:08:01.515
do you think that the same thing is going to happen with Jon Snow?

00:08:01.515 --> 00:08:03.740
Like they'll both end up choosing family over duty.

00:08:03.740 --> 00:08:05.535
I mean I would really love to see that.

00:08:05.535 --> 00:08:07.534
It'd be a very human choice to make.

00:08:07.534 --> 00:08:11.735
Humans are flawed so as much as Jon wants to uphold the ideals that he believes in

00:08:11.735 --> 00:08:14.913
he's probably going to make the emotional choice at a certain point.

00:08:14.913 --> 00:08:19.614
All in all great episode. I know a lot of people were disappointed in the first episode just because

00:08:19.614 --> 00:08:22.693
it moved a little slowly and they just spent so much time just setting stuff up

00:08:22.693 --> 00:08:26.567
but now I feel like we're actually moving forward. We're moving all these plot lines forward.

00:08:26.567 --> 00:08:29.800
Just a reminder I'll announce the winner in my Q&amp;A tomorrow

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:32.334
so be sure to subscribe to get that if you haven't already.

00:08:32.334 --> 00:08:36.014
All you have to do to enter the giveaway is be a subscriber and leave a comment. Nice and simple.

00:08:36.014 --> 00:08:41.114
I haven't decided what my bonus video is going to be for next week so feel free to leave me a request in the comments.

00:08:41.114 --> 00:08:45.653
Maybe something Dorne-ish if we're going to be seeing more of the Martells. Hopefully we'll see more of the Martells next week.

